---
import { FACTS } from "../data/facts";

const features = [
  { icon: "context", title: "Context that gets smarter", desc: "The lossless DAG context engine is the default - full history kept, details recalled on demand via ctx_search / ctx_inspect. Dead content eviction, observation masking, LLM compaction with 3-level fallback, and progressive tool disclosure that loads detailed guidance only when needed. Prefer the classic multi-stage pipeline? Switch modes with one config reload - reversible, no restart, no data loss. Your agents never forget what matters." },
  { icon: "automate", title: "Automate your mornings", desc: "Graph pipelines run multi-step workflows on a schedule. Scan the news, summarize your email, check your calendar, compile a briefing, deliver it to Telegram at 8am." },
  { icon: "tools", title: "Built-in tools, plus the whole MCP ecosystem", desc: `Built-in tools cover file ops, web search, browser automation, media processing, and a sandboxed shell - and you can plug in ${FACTS.mcp}. GitHub, Gmail, Notion, PostgreSQL, and the rest live in that ecosystem; Comis bundles zero MCP servers, you pick exactly what you trust. Shell commands run inside an OS-level filesystem sandbox so agents can only access their own workspace.` },
  { icon: "media", title: "Voice and media, naturally", desc: "Send a voice note, get a text reply. Analyze images with vision models. Transcribe audio with Whisper, Groq, or Deepgram. Generate speech with OpenAI, ElevenLabs, or Edge TTS." },
  { icon: "models", title: "Any model, your choice", desc: `${FACTS.models}. Different agents can use different models, and the security floor never moves - the sandbox, credential broker, and content scanner apply identically whether you run a frontier cloud model or a local Qwen or Gemma. Comis tunes itself to the model, too: an immutable capability profile keeps the prompt inside what a small model can actually use (focused tool sets, prompt-size budgets, deterministic tool selection) and adds reliability rails for how small models fail - goal re-anchoring, a poison-resistant recall floor, tool-call JSON repair with self-correction, and reasoning models' chain-of-thought kept out of the reply. Weaker model, stricter lockdown, more scaffolding - and capable models pay nothing for it. No vendor lock-in.` },
  { icon: "memory", title: "Memory that persists", desc: "SQLite with FTS5 full-text search and vector embeddings. An on-device cross-encoder reranker re-reads candidates against the question for relevance - it turns on automatically when its model is present, and downloads nothing out of the box; an optional entity lane brings back associatively related memories. Contradictions resolve by trust first, then recency - a verified fact wins over a newer low-trust claim, without deleting history. Repeated facts consolidate into corroborated observations whose proof accrues across runs, and an opt-in feedback loop lets recall learn from which memories actually got used. Trust-partitioned and trust-ranked recall prevents memory poisoning - all on-device." },
  { icon: "key", title: "Credential broker", desc: "Drive any API-key CLI - Claude Code included - with the key kept out of the sandbox. The real key lives in the daemon's encrypted store and is injected at the network boundary, never inside the sandbox where the agent runs; the CLI authenticates while your key stays in the daemon. Add a new tool by dropping its key in the broker - no narrow, hardcoded provider list." },
];
---

<section class="px-6 py-20 md:py-28 bg-navy-light/50">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
    <p class="text-teal font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">What you can do</p>
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-14">
      Real tools. Real workflows. Real results.
    </h2>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
      {features.map((f) => (
        <div class="bg-navy/80 border border-white/5 rounded-xl p-8">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">{f.title}</h3>
          <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">{f.desc}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
